- What tests ensure rollback can restore previous connectivity without downtime?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design automated IR in Azure at scale, integrating Key Vault, Sentinel, Runbooks, and network isolation.

## Key Concepts

- Key Vault rotation and secret versioning
- Azure Sentinel detection rules and alerting
- Automation Runbooks or Logic Apps
- Private Endpoints and NSGs
- Azure AD session revocation and PIM

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-IR runbook snippet (Azure SDK)
async function rotateSecret(vaultName, secretName){
  const newValue = generateSecret();
  await secretClient.setSecret(vaultName, secretName, newValue);
  await aadClient.revokeUserSessions('compromised-id');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the rollback path under partial failure?
- How do you ensure no downtime during rotation?

## Why This Is Asked

To assess practical cross-tenant crypto governance, KMS design, and audit controls in Azure for enterprise buyers like Oracle, MongoDB, Hugging Face.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant KEKs in Azure Key Vault
- Envelope encryption with DEKs
- RBAC and data masking
- Auditing and rollback planning

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: fetch tenant DEK from Key Vault and wrap data
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require('@azure/identity');
const { KeyClient, CryptographyClient } = require('@azure/keyvault-keys');

const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
const keyClient = new KeyClient(`https://${vaultName}.vault.azure.net`, credential);
const key = await keyClient.getKey(tenantDekName);
const cryptoClient = new CryptographyClient(key.id, credential);
const wrapped = await cryptoClient.wrapKey('RSA-OAEP', dek);
```

